# Module: api_client
Compile unit for the Forum Frontend.
Generates: `frontend/src/api_client.ts` (new module — replaces the mock data layer `data.ts` when the real backend lands)

## Role
The frontend's single seam to the backend: every HTTP call and Realtime subscription lives here, so swapping mock ↔ live is a one-module change.

## Interface
- `getFeatures({ view, sort, q, status })` → GET `/api/features`
- `getFeature(id)` → GET `/api/features/{id}`
- `getMyFeatures()` → GET `/api/features/mine`
- `createFeature({ title, description })` → POST `/api/features` (expect `202` + `feature_id`; surface `429` as out-of-coins)
- `upvote(id)` → POST `/api/features/{id}/upvote` (surface `409` as already-hyped)
- `reboot(id)` → POST `/api/features/{id}/reboot`
- `getBroadcast(limit)` → GET `/api/broadcast`
- `getSandbox()` → GET `/api/sandbox`
- `subscribe({ onFeatureInsert, onBroadcastEvent, onDeployment })` — Supabase Realtime on `feature_requests`, `broadcast_events`, `deployments`

## Behavior
- **Conforms to `prompts/shared/openapi.yaml`** (the frozen wire contract, snake_case): request/response bodies match its schemas exactly; test against a spec-driven mock server.
- **Wire → view-model mapping lives here and only here.** The components use view names that differ from wire names; this module owns the translation so neither side drifts:
  `description` → `scope` · `unlock_threshold` → `needed` · `created_at` → `createdAt` · `shipped_at`/`shipped_version` → `shippedAt`/`shippedVersion` · `merge_count` → `mergeCount` · `ai_explanation` → `aiExplanation` · `postpone_count` → `holdCycle` (with `holdMax` = 2 constant) · `author_handle` → `author` · `viewer_has_voted` → seeds `votedIds`.
  Supabase Realtime rows arrive in wire shape (raw columns); pass them through the same mapper before they reach components.
- `429` responses carry `resets_at` — feed it to the coin-refresh countdown instead of the mock's hardcoded window.
- Base URL + Supabase credentials from Vite env; when absent, export the mock implementation (current `data.ts` behavior) so the app stays standalone.
- Attach the Supabase Auth JWT to writes; reads are anonymous.
- Never talk to Redis or Postgres directly — HTTP API + Realtime only (manifest boundary rule).
- Errors return the backend's friendly copy verbatim for direct display; never leak raw payloads.

## Testing convention
Unit tests use **Vitest** + **React Testing Library** + **jsdom** (Vite-native; not Jest). This module is the single backend seam, so component modules are tested against a **stubbed `api_client`** (mock each method) or a spec-driven mock server from `openapi.yaml` — never a live backend. Realtime is mocked by invoking the `subscribe` callbacks (`onFeatureInsert`/`onBroadcastEvent`/`onDeployment`) directly. No unit test hits a live backend or Supabase Realtime.

